<p><em>I read, and reread the required reading, so I hope I didn't miss any crucial steps! I'm new to all of this.</em></p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Not currently, still in the very beginning stages.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror, Drama/Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The core idea of this SCP is a child with C-PTSD from an unstable/abusive home life has developed anomalous properties, seemingly as a self-defense mechanism.</li>
<li>The child unknowingly manifests horrors that protect her in her sleep, but only in the event she has a nightmare.</li>
<li>The manifestation of these monsters will attack any other lifeform that comes within 3 meters of her as she slumbers.</li>
<li>The moment the child awakens from her nightmare, the monsters vanish, and the child is left with no inclination of what she has done - only that she's had a bad dream.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The child has been taken into Foundation care in an attempt to not only learn about her anomalies and why they seemingly manifested, and try to pinpoint what made these anomalies manifest in the first place.</p>
<p>Through trial and error the researchers assigned to her case begin to understand her condition, learn how to avoid potential manifestations of her monstrous protectors, and attempt to rehabilitate her in the process.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
The SCP within this story is just a normal little girl, who doesn't understand what is happening to her or why. She has no idea of her anomaly, only that she was &quot;taken away&quot; from her parents. <em>This part I'm mildly struggling with. I feel like I have a good start here, I'm just not sure how to make this SCP stand out against thousands of others.</em></p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
I have a good idea of what this SCP is, and what she can do, but I need a bit of help figuring out the specifics of her story. This is my first attempt at writing an SCP, and I want to make sure it's air tight before I even consider sending in a draft for serious critique. I have her containment procedures mapped out, and a bit of her description, but I'm unsure if what I have so far is even reasonable. I appreciate any assistance.</p>

